{"id":1432,"date":"2020-11-27T16:41:23","date_gmt":"2020-11-28T00:41:23","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1432"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:40:35","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:40:35","slug":"program-the-remote-control","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/program-the-remote-control\/","title":{"rendered":"Program the Remote Control"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2216245c516\" name=\"6a2216245c516\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Briefing video<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]This video goes over how to program the remote, but you still need to go through the lesson![\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=1iONymFnno0&#8243; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2216245c68b\" name=\"6a2216245c68b\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Remote control and library<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Right before void setup(), include the Smart Inventor library.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;SmartInventor.h&gt;<\/pre>\n<p>Inside void setup(), enter the code below so you can actually use the remote control.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">SmartInventor.TVRemoconUse();<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2216245c700\" name=\"6a2216245c700\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Baud rate<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Make sure to include the baud rate so there is serial communication with the Smart Inventor Board.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">Serial.begin(57600);<\/pre>\n<p>Baud rate review time!\u00a0This function creates a high-transfer\u00a0baud\u00a0connection between the\u00a0remote control\u00a0and the\u00a0Smart Inventor Board.\u00a0A higher baud number means the board will process information faster, but there&#8217;s also a higher chance for errors.\u00a0A lower\u00a0baud number means the board will process information slower, but there will also be less of a chance for errors.<\/p>\n<p>Baud rates range anywhere from 300 to 250000. Make sure that your baud rate is a number that is found within the drop-down menu in the lower righthand corner of the serial monitor.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2216245c756\" name=\"6a2216245c756\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Delay<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Include a delay of 500 milliseconds in void setup() so the Smart Inventor board can check for entries from the remote control.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">delay(500);<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2216245c7a7\" name=\"6a2216245c7a7\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Read the remote control<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]You can move on to void loop() now! Create a variable named keyData to represent data being read from the remote control. This variable will also store information about the last button that was pressed.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">int keyData = SmartInventor.TVRemoconData();<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2216245c7fe\" name=\"6a2216245c7fe\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>The up button<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Obviously you want the buttons on your remote control to do something. Figure out a way to make this happen in Arduino! Spoiler alert: if, else if, and else statements. Take a look at the example below!<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">if(keyData==KEY_U)\r\n{\r\n    \/\/ACTION\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>The first if statement you&#8217;re going to tackle is about the up button. Use the code below to have your program say &#8220;UP&#8221; when you press the up button (it&#8217;s KEY_U here).<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">if(keyData==KEY_U)\r\n{\r\n    Serial.println(\"UP\");\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2216245c84a\" name=\"6a2216245c84a\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>The down button<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Next, have your program say &#8220;DOWN&#8221; when you press your remote control&#8217;s down button. Since you already used an if statement for the up button, you need to use an else if statement for this part.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">else if(keyData==KEY_D)\r\n{\r\n    Serial.println(\"DOWN\");\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2216245c898\" name=\"6a2216245c898\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>No buttons are pressed<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]There might be times when you&#8217;re not pressing the remote control&#8217;s buttons at all! For those cases, use an else statement to have your program say &#8220;NOTHING&#8221;.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">else\r\n{\r\n    Serial.println(\"NOTHING\");\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2216245c8ff\" name=\"6a2216245c8ff\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 9<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Final code<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]This is what your final code should look like:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;SmartInventor.h&gt; \/\/ Include library \r\n \r\nvoid setup() {    \r\n    SmartInventor.TVRemoconUse(); \/\/ Initializes use of remote control    \r\n    Serial.begin(57600); \/\/Establishes serial connection    \r\n    delay(500); \/\/Indicates time step to allow time for processing}\r\n \r\nvoid loop() {\r\n    int keyData = SmartInventor.TVRemoconData();\r\n    if (keyData == KEY_U)\r\n    {\r\n        Serial.println(\"UP\");\r\n    }\r\n    else if (keyData == KEY_D)\r\n    {\r\n        Serial.println(\"DOWN\");\r\n    }\r\n    else\r\n    {\r\n        Serial.println(\"NOTHING\");\r\n    }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>Up for a challenge? Program actions for all of the other\u00a0<strong>buttons<\/strong>\u00a0on the\u00a0<strong>remote control<\/strong>!<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>KEY_U<\/li>\n<li>KEY_D<\/li>\n<li>KEY_L<\/li>\n<li>KEY_R<\/li>\n<li>KEY_C<\/li>\n<li>KEY_F1<\/li>\n<li>KEY_F2<\/li>\n<li>KEY_F3<\/li>\n<li>KEY_F4<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 10 Briefing video [vc_column_text]This video goes over how to program the remote, but you still need to go through the lesson![\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=\"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=1iONymFnno0\" align=\"center\"] [\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column] Step 11 Remote control&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/program-the-remote-control\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1736,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":802,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1760,1817,1753,1777,1808,1770,1793,423,626,1533,1438,853,144,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2163,2218,2173,2123,2122,2111,2172,2171,2190],"class_list":["post-1432","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-computer-science","lesson-tag-electronics","lesson-tag-fundamentals","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-remote-control","lesson-tag-robotics","lesson-tag-rokit-smart","lesson-tag-trailer","module-trailer","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1432","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":2,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1432\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1737,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1432\/revisions\/1737"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1736"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1432"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=1432"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=1432"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","hr